+        // How FAR does repair move things?
+        //
+        // The log has always reported only a COUNT ("relocated 11790"), which
+        // says nothing about whether this pass is benign. It matters: the
+        // measured critical path on this design is a flop-to-flop net with no
+        // logic between the endpoints, whose two flops sit 132 slice rows apart
+        // (SLICE_X5Y137 -> SLICE_X26Y269, logic 0.322 ns, net 15.104 ns).
+        //
+        // The ring search below is bounded by max(gw, gh) -- the whole device --
+        // and takes the first valid bel at the smallest radius without regard to
+        // where the cell's neighbours are. A cell that cannot be placed locally
+        // can therefore legitimately end up anywhere, and a count would not show
+        // it. These buckets do.
